# Nix build symlinks, anchored to the repository root so the pattern cannot
# reach into a subdirectory. Unanchored `result-*` swallowed three
# `contracts/examples/runner-rpc/` fixtures named `result-*.json` — they were
# never committed, so `contracts-test` in CI validated a smaller fixture set
# than it did locally, including the one guarding D26's sequence gap-checking.
/result
/result-*

# The same symlinks, one directory down: `nix build` run from `contracts/`
# writes them there, and both were committed before the pattern existed. A
# stray disk image was tracked at the root too.
/contracts/result
/contracts/result-*
/neuman.qcow2
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.ruff_cache/
/target/
.direnv/
.#*
# Editor scratch files. An agent's file-writing tool leaves these beside the
# file it is editing, and they are near-copies of real source — so an untracked
# one is both noise in `git status` and a thing that can be committed by
# accident, which is worse: the flake builds from the git tree, so a stale
# duplicate of a module would be visible to the build.
.neuman-*

# Write-reach probes. Neuman writes a 2-byte `.probe` to confirm a directory is
# writable, and under a profile that denies unlink it cannot remove its own
# marker (N109 is the same shape one layer down). Ignored rather than deleted
# repeatedly: the file is evidence the sandbox is working, and a dirty tree
# after every session is noise.
.probe
.wtest

# Debian packages built by deploy/ubuntu/build.sh. The released artifact goes
# to the project site, not into this repository.
/deploy/ubuntu/*.deb

# `pip wheel` and `pip install` write these into the source tree.
/build/
/*/build/
